{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Dream With Me and Sinatra, With Love fit my interest in expressive, polished vocals and melodic accompaniment, which connects with Stages and my classical crossover listening.",
    "CLASSICAL GAS appeals to my interest in instrumental music after my recent relaxing classical selection, although I would expect something livelier."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me connects with my past Christmas listening, but seasonal music does not fit what I want right now.",
    "The Pirates of the Caribbean soundtrack feels too intense for my current quieter mood, while Album Number Two and The Mountain give me too little information to judge whether they fit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past interest in Christmas music seems to have been treated as an ongoing desire for seasonal listening.",
    "My country and soundtrack listening seems to have been carried forward without enough attention to whether those albums offer the gentle vocal or instrumental experience I want today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest relaxing classical selection matters because I am currently drawn toward calmer listening, even though I have enjoyed other moods before.",
    "A possible match is not always something I would choose now: I would sample Alone in Iz World, and Partners interests me only if it is the vocal duets album I recognize."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my taste for melodic vocals and instrumental music, but only partly captured my current preference for quieter, nonseasonal listening."
}"}
